add(360,'Classify raw journal compatibility before resume','Resume admission MUST invoke the landed journal compatibility classifier on raw source-journal bytes before allowing replay or new dispatch.','C144 C175','P09-C established dropped unknown-kind effect rows re-executed while classifier reports unsupported; hx exports verifies classifier exists but partial references cannot establish absence, which is bounded to grep call-site surface in C144.', ['Assert a journal with dropped node/unknown-kind rows is refused before new node/provider dispatch and exposes the compatibility verdict plus bounded warning.','Assert compatible settled read/agent journal still replays according to its basis and unclassified readable rows remain fail-closed.'], 'journal/p09-runtime.probe.ts dropped-effect-row case plus test/workflow-journal-compat.test.ts; raw bytes/readJournal/classifyJournal oracle','V3','W12/W21 compatibility/MNI P09',(),prior=('EAT-R256',))
add(361,'Explain the first replay decline','A workflow resume MUST expose the first typed reason that a recorded prefix cannot be replayed before or at its first newly paid agent call.','C136 C137 C159','P09-D/P08/probe3 established silent decline across basis, failed entry, edited prompt, resumed journal and replay-unsafe cases; C136 establishes the 2001-path cap and nonrepo decline, not that replacing it with a cheap hash is safe.', ['Assert control same-basis replay reports replayed count; each named decline emits one reason with position and changed basis dimension when known.','Assert launch text counts recorded candidates, not guaranteed hits; >2000-path/non-Git unknown basis reports measured-unavailable rather than claiming cache hit.','Assert the reason is present in both workflow log and notification without repeating an unbounded error payload.'], 'journal/p09-runtime.probe.ts D, p08-silent-decline.probe.ts, p14-replay-cap.probe.ts and node-rpc/probe3-declined-journal oracle','V3','W12 replay transparency/MNI P09',(),conditions='Removing the 2000-path cap and bare-resume argument inheritance are separate deferred obligations; conservative replay admission is preserved.')
